{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden-render character-regression case matrix (docs/design/testing-strategy.md §4,",
    "docs/design/dsp-engine.md §9; task plan/backlog/026-golden-harness.md).",
    "Each case renders tests/golden/inputs/<input> with mwstime-render --case and is",
    "compared against tests/golden/blessed/<id>.wav by golden_compare.",
    "",
    "Schema (per tools/mwstime-render/Cases.h, plus harness-only top-level keys the",
    "loader ignores):",
    "  id      : unique; the blessed file is <id>.wav (the <model>_<case> convention).",
    "  input   : a file in tests/golden/inputs/.",
    "  model   : s900|s950|s1000|s1100.",
    "  params  : any subset of the dsp-engine §2 render flags; omitted = §2 default.",
    "  bitDepth: 16|24|32|float (default 16). Goldens use 16-bit so every blessed WAV",
    "            stays well under 1 MB (plain git, no LFS); 16-bit exact compare is",
    "            valid because the renderer is deterministic.",
    "  policy  : exact|tolerance (harness only). 'exact' = CLASSIC stretch-only",
    "            (transpose 0, character OFF) integer path -> bit-exact on all",
    "            platforms (dsp-engine §3.2). 'tolerance' = float-stage cases ->",
    "            bit-exact on the reference platform (macOS arm64), tol 1e-6 off it.",
    "  note    : human description (harness only).",
    "",
    "LEGAL: all inputs are original synthetic material (tools/gen_golden_inputs/);",
    "there is NO copyrighted audio in this repo (no Amen break)."
  ],
